Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.05,0:00:05.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,STRK20 reaches the outside world through one primitive.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.22,0:00:08.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Two protocol rules shape everything downstream.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.85,0:00:12.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,At most one external call per pool transaction.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.14,0:00:16.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And every token's balance must end at exactly zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.44,0:00:23.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Together they mean a private action is only as expressive as\Nthe single helper contract it calls.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.32,0:00:24.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Want a private swap?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.67,0:00:27.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Deploy and audit a swap helper.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.28,0:00:28.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Lend?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.11,0:00:29.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Another one.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.17,0:00:30.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Swap, then lend?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.42,0:00:31.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,A third.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.31,0:00:34.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every new interaction is a new Cairo contract.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.49,0:00:39.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,That is why almost everything built on STRK20 today is a\Npayment app.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.88,0:00:43.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Payments are the only thing you can ship without writing\NCairo.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.97,0:00:48.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Jalin is one helper that takes a plan instead of fixed\Nparameters.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.65,0:00:51.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,A plan is a bounded list of steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.41,0:00:57.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each step names a target, a selector, calldata, and the\Napprovals it needs.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.10,0:01:08.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Jalin runs them in order inside the single privacy invoke,\Ncredits each declared output, enforces the floor the caller\Nset on it, and hands the deposits back to the pool.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.81,0:01:10.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nothing is whitelisted.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.41,0:01:15.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Any Starknet contract is a valid target and the calldata is\Nfree form.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.54,0:01:21.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,That is what makes a bridge call, a DEX route, and a lending\Ndeposit the same object.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.40,0:01:22.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,A plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.29,0:01:27.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Composition moves inside the single invoke, where the protocol\Nallows it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.51,0:01:35.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Free calldata sounds unsafe, so safety is carried by\Ninvariants in Cairo rather than by a whitelist.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.36,0:01:38.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,The router holds nothing between transactions.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.29,0:01:41.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Anything left on it is unreachable.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.09,0:01:48.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,That is why each output can be credited its whole balance\Ninstead of a measured delta, and it is one less thing to get\Nwrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.82,0:01:52.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,This runs on Starknet mainnet against the live pool.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.50,0:01:56.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Here is one of its transactions being checked against the\Nchain right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.70,0:02:00.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,The page reads the receipt and answers four questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.45,0:02:08.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Does it exist, did it succeed, did it touch the STRK20 pool,\Nand did it run through our own contract.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.19,0:02:14.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It reads a whole submission too, and beside its own verdict it\Nshows the sprint hub's.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.03,0:02:18.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Three transactions, all counted, and the two agree.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.11,0:02:22.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,This endpoint answers for any team's repository, not just\Nours.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.85,0:02:32.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Another team already took a mainnet measurement from our\Ndocumentation and caught a seven day window in their own code\Nthat would have closed in three hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.79,0:02:36.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,One general router instead of a new contract per interaction.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.50,0:02:44.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cairo tests, a published SDK, a threat model, and every claim\Non this page verifiable against mainnet.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.95,0:02:45.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Jalin.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.83,0:02:48.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,To weave separate strands into one.
